WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:03.303
[airplane roars]

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:07.907
WOMAN ON INTERCOM: Welcome
to Hartfield-Jackson

00:00:07.974 --> 00:00:09.542
Atlanta International Airport.

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:15.582
We're looking
through the LOB, left

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:21.321
over bags that passengers left
out there for whatever reason.

00:00:21.388 --> 00:00:24.924
When passengers leave bags,
we gotta go through them, make

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:27.627
sure there's nothing illegal.

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:28.995
OFFICER AMADOR:
Depending on the day,

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:31.731
you can get about 30, 40 LOBs.

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:33.400
They are the people
that are in a hurry,

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:35.101
and they think they're
going to miss the flight,

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:37.537
and they'd rather
leave the bag behind.

00:00:37.604 --> 00:00:40.807
Or the reason we
check, the person

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:42.976
might not want to get
caught bringing something

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:45.445
and leave the bag behind.

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:47.113
OFFICER MAINOR: When
I go through the bags,

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.815
I try and be methodical.

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:50.850
I try not to overlook anything.

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:52.452
[bags rustling]

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:56.356
Coffee beans.

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:59.325
I can't really see inside it.

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:02.362
I'mma have to cut it open.

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:07.534
Got a coffee smell, but
we'll see what we got.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:11.104
[suspense music]

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:19.813
Coffee is supposed
to be brown, right?

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:26.186
OFFICER MAINOR: Coffee is
not supposed to be white.

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:33.760
[theme music]

00:01:39.065 --> 00:01:40.767
Now we just cut open
the rest and see.

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:47.340
And again.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:53.513
Oh, wow.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:55.915
OK.

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:57.417
Try not to get too
high or too low

00:01:57.484 --> 00:01:58.785
because you know
you got to test it.

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:00.854
But when you start
seeing the same thing,

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.689
you're like, oh, OK.

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:03.623
That's not the norm.

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:10.563
OFFICER SMILEY: No, he didn't.
MALE 2: Oh, yes he did.

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:11.698
[chuckles]

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:13.166
OFFICER SMILEY: So this
was inside the coffee?

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:14.067
OFFICER MAINOR: Mm-hm.

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:15.435
OFFICER SMILEY: Gotcha.

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:17.837
So do they look, like,
commercially packaged?

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:19.172
OFFICER MAINOR Yeah.

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:21.641
It looked legit because
see how it's stitched?

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:23.676
Sometimes you just
can't skip steps.

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:24.577
It's that simple.

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:25.478
It's that easy.

00:02:27.881 --> 00:02:31.351
So now we're going to test
it and see what we have.

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:36.523
MALE 3: What do you think?

00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:38.992
OFFICER MAINOR: Mm-hm.

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:42.228
[suspense music]

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:51.704
Hold on.

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:52.405
It's hot.

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:53.606
MALE 3: There you go.

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:56.743
It's reading
cocaine hydrochloride,

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:59.479
so that's cocaine.

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:01.180
It's just straight cocaine.

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:02.949
No mixture, no nothing else.

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:05.785
You know, it's a good day.

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:08.521
OFFICER SMILEY: Nice catch.

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:12.158
[music playing]

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:20.700
OFFICER MAINOR: 3.51 kilos.

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:27.674
Yeah.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:28.841
That's a lot.

00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:29.976
Since I've been
here, this is one

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:31.077
of the largest ones we've had.

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:32.145
That's over a year and a half.

